From de595dbf90d758ec6b73cf40ec4f8f63e0c4f498 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bateske <kevin@bateske.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:19:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] CHSd P3: the simulator's card checks the bus rule and
 takes card timing knobs

Any sd:: call while a flush holds SPI1 is now a BUG: line (sim_flushActive()
reads the flush state without moving virtual time). Card timing comes
from CHSD_SIM_CMD_US, _BLK_US, _READ_US, _JITTER_US, _COLD_US/_COLD_KB,
_FAIL_EVERY and _INIT_US (defaults: the old timing). As on the board, a
streamed block reaches fn once the next block's token is in, and a card
pulled and put back needs init() before stream()/recover() work again.
The three SD games' scripts give pixel-identical frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
